These FLAC files are part of this repository and under its MIT licence (see LICENSE at the root).

The audio is synthetic: it is generated by the tests' own integer-only signal code in src/flac/synth.rs, so it is the same on every platform, and no recorded audio is in them. Each file was encoded once from that PCM with the reference FLAC encoder (flac 1.5.0, --no-padding, with the block size, order and stereo options its name gives). expected.txt holds the 64-bit hash of each file's decoded PCM.

Their Matroska and MP4 remuxes live in tests/refs/flac: examples/record_refs writes them from these files with this crate's own Matroska and MP4 writers (`cargo run --release --example record_refs -- flac`).
